00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.650
So Container Builder is
a cloud-hosted service

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.627
for doing builds.

00:07:43.627 --> 00:07:45.460
And it originally, it
was created for Docker

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.070
build specifically,
so it was a way

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.440
to build Docker images
without actually having

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.880
to have Docker on your
machine, in a sort

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:58.500
of consistent, reliable, fast,
scalable cloud-hosted service.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.600
And as for scarce integrations
with Google Container Registry.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.322
So you're able to set
up build triggers.

00:08:03.322 --> 00:08:05.530
So essentially, you make a
change to the source code,

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:08.440
set up a trigger, trigger
build that happens in the cloud

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.944
and then gets deposited into
a registry or artifact store.

00:08:10.944 --> 00:08:11.860
FRANSESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.550
