00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.460
FRANSESC CAMPOY:
So I'm wondering,

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:41.990
since we've been talking
a lot about build steps,

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:47.280
and those build steps, for me,
they're not always building.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.060
For instance, if I had
a Go application, what

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:55.310
I want to do with a tool
like this is to run Lint

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.520
and to make sure
that there's no bugs,

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:01.370
I want to run all my unit tests
and then finally build it.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.950
All of these things
are easily integrated

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:07.849
with Container Builder, but
then what about extra things?

00:17:07.849 --> 00:17:10.490
Like let's say I want
