00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:14.150
once my new image
has been created.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:17.930
How easy is it to deploy it
to App Engine to a new version

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.220
and run some testings there?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.079
Is this part of what
you try to cover,

00:17:22.079 --> 00:17:24.890
or is this something that should
be done with a different tool?

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.431
DAVID BENDORY: So
this starts getting

00:17:26.431 --> 00:17:29.120
into the line of where the
builder, as a component

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.770
of your continuous integration,
ends and other tools begin.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.080
We do have users who
do some of the things

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:38.180
you're describing using
Container Builder.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:41.170
We certainly have
users who are linting,

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:43.162
users who are
running unit tests,

00:17:43.162 --> 00:17:45.245
we have users who are
playing with Docker Compose,

00:17:45.245 --> 00:17:46.940
so that at the end
of their build,

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.100
they compose an
environment and run

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.690
some simple tests against it.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:52.979
But for a really true
Integration Suite,

00:17:52.979 --> 00:17:54.770
I think Christopher
wants to talk about one

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.771
of the other products
that we offer.

00:17:57.771 --> 00:17:59.280
CHRISTOPHER SANSON:
Yeah, I think

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.940
when you're talking about
production level and stage

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:05.810
rollouts, and any sort of
reliable uptime service,

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:09.020
we offer Spinnaker as our
recommended continuous delivery

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.530
tool.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.860
So as David said before,
your container builder

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.490
would build your
Docker image, push it

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:18.620
to a registry or some other JAR
file, artifact, what have you.

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:20.120
And then you would
set up Spinnaker,

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:23.300
to listen to the presence of
that new release candidate

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:26.329
and then trigger a
deployment pipeline.

00:18:26.329 --> 00:18:27.870
