So the first thing you do is
you start these Linux instance

00:29:42.850 --> 00:29:45.460
and then you install Python
and then you instant Tornado

00:29:45.460 --> 00:29:48.880
and then you install Futures and
then you download ImageMagick.

00:29:48.880 --> 00:29:51.539
You install it too, and then
once you're ready to go,

00:29:51.539 --> 00:29:52.330
you start running--

00:29:52.330 --> 00:29:52.890
MARK MANDEL: Oh wow.

00:29:52.890 --> 00:29:53.410
Yeah.

00:29:53.410 --> 00:29:55.201
FRANSESC CAMPOY: There's
a bunch of things.

00:29:55.201 --> 00:29:57.050
And that takes,
according to him,

00:29:57.050 --> 00:30:00.380
it takes around 75 seconds,
something like that.

00:30:00.380 --> 00:30:03.570
And then he says, well instead
of doing that, let's create

00:30:03.570 --> 00:30:04.830
a custom image.

00:30:04.830 --> 00:30:09.030
And then the startup time
goes from around 75 seconds

00:30:09.030 --> 00:30:09.987
to under one second.

00:30:09.987 --> 00:30:11.070
MARK MANDEL: That's crazy.

00:30:11.070 --> 00:30:13.389
FRANSESC CAMPOY: Actually,
it's under 20 milliseconds.

00:30:13.389 --> 00:30:15.180
MARK MANDEL: Well,
that's the startup time.

00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:16.888
FRANSESC CAMPOY: That's
the startup time.

00:30:16.888 --> 00:30:20.340
Yeah, but you actually
went from crazy 75 seconds

00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:23.267
on top of the provisioning
time to just 20 milliseconds

00:30:23.267 --> 00:30:24.600
on top of the provisioning time.

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:26.410
So you're actually
gaining a lot of time.

00:30:26.410 --> 00:30:27.360
MARK MANDEL: You're
gaining a lot of time

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:28.280
there, which is really cool.

00:30:28.280 --> 00:30:29.580
FRANSESC CAMPOY: So it's
definitely worth checking out.

00:30:29.580 --> 00:30:31.410
